# Code comments (not docstrings)

Default: **no new comments**. Prefer clearer names, smaller functions, and
tests over narration. Required API/module **docstrings** and **JSDoc** stay
under language or project rules — this rule owns `//`, `#`, and block comments
only.

## Refuse (do not leave these in source)

- Ephemeral agent trails: "changed for X", "temporary", "quick fix",
  "TODO for this session", "Blank = … so I can …"
- Restating the next line or an obvious control-flow choice
- Changelog / blame notes ("fixed null check", "per review", ticket keys as
  the whole comment)
- Commented-out dead code kept "just in case"
- Speculative or soon-stale guidance (env workarounds, one-off operator steps)

Put short-lived explanation in the **chat reply**, commit body, or tracker —
not in the file.

## Allow (sparingly)

Only when a future reader cannot recover the *why* from code + docs/tests:

- Non-obvious invariant, hazard, or compatibility constraint that must stay
- Mandatory markers a tool or gate requires
- A durable operator note in an **example** env/template when peers already
  use that pattern — never a session diary

If unsure whether a comment is durable: **omit it**.

## When editing

- Do not add comments as a habit while coding or "documenting" a quick change
- Prefer deleting stale or ephemeral comments you touch over rewriting them
- Do not expand nearby comments unless the user asked for documentation
